00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:48.500
Usually, it says
Custom Domains on it.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:50.180
But that was taken out.

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:54.430
And then we can Add a
domain mapping here.

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:56.770
And a domain mapping takes
two things, of course--

00:18:56.770 --> 00:19:01.990
what service should accept
traffic coming to this URL?

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:05.770
And then what domain
should catch these?

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:09.190
So of course, here,
we would set up

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:10.990
just as you do with
any other service,

00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:13.420
like App Engine
or anything else.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:15.460
You would set up
a verified domain

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:17.740
and walk through the steps
here in Cloud Platform

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:19.300
to verify the domain.

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:23.050
And when you're done, now,
your new custom domain

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:26.895
points to this service.

00:19:26.895 --> 00:19:27.520
GRANT: Awesome.

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:29.960
